Method: read-only, actual view_image inspection of all six original PNGs; verified their bytes against corresponding screenshot_sha256 and PNG dimensions. No SDK/test/native launch/GUI operation. The reviewer did not view the MP4 in this review.

DIRECTLY VISIBLE IN THE SIX ORIGINAL IMAGES
1. ai-draft-before-close.png: Chinese, light full Trail window; AI task surface shows new task / waiting state, draft “D2_AI_DRAFT_CLOSE_PROTECTION：保留这段未发送草稿。” and a Send to AI control. Bottom status reports AI task and paused manual input. No transcript, approval card, or dialog is visible.
2. ai-draft-after-close-no-confirmation.png: same titled application window and one visible tab; content is a bare trail-prd% raw terminal prompt. The former AI draft surface and a confirmation dialog are not visible in this sampled frame. The truncated identical profile label and ⌘1 shortcut do not establish which numeric session survived.
3. composer-draft-before-close.png: Blocks reports 0 blocks, the Command composer contains printf 'D2_COMPOSER_DRAFT_CLOSE_PROTECTION\n', Shell ready is visible, and Run is enabled. The draft is in the editor rather than output. No confirmation dialog is visible.
4. composer-draft-after-close-no-confirmation.png: raw trail-prd% terminal prompt replaces the sampled Command surface; one tab remains visible, with no draft or current confirmation dialog. Pixels alone do not establish draft deletion versus switching to another session.
5. secondary-click-before.png: one tab with two panes. Left Blocks pane has the active blue boundary, zero blocks, and printf 'D2_RIGHT_CLICK_TARGET_DRAFT\n' in the Command editor; Run is enabled. Right raw terminal is visibly dimmed/inactive. Bottom status identifies Blocks/manual input.
6. secondary-click-after-target-switched.png: same two-pane arrangement. The blue active boundary and active header controls are now on the right raw terminal; the left output area is dimmed and its Run control is disabled. The original left command draft remains readable and unchanged. No context menu is visible in this sampled frame. Bottom status now identifies terminal/manual input.

METADATA / OPERATOR-DEPENDENT FACTS (NOT CLAIMED FROM PIXELS)
All six JSON sidecars bind capture to app PID 68899 and window ID 29753. Window bounds are 1728×1084 logical screen units and originals are 3456×2168 pixels. This does not constitute cross-display DPI acceptance.
The four draft-close captures report active_pids=[] and frontmost_pid=71653, so they are normal application window captures while this App was inactive. Both secondary-click captures report active_pids=[68899], frontmost_pid=68899. No claim is made about foreground state between these sampled instants.
AI before process subtree contains zsh PID 69040 on ttys014; AI after contains zsh PID 77120 on ttys017 and no 69040. Composer before contains 77120; Composer after contains 78118 on ttys014 and no 77120. These are discrete process samples: they support replacement/removal at those times, not a continuous assertion that no transient processes existed.
Both secondary-click process samples contain zsh PIDs 78118/79498 with ttys014/ttys017, respectively. Their unchanged sampled presence supports no shell recreation across this observed transition; numeric active-session mapping comes from operator observations, not the pane ordinal labels.
reproduction-notes.json explicitly identifies itself as root transcription from CUA outputs, not raw AX export. It reports close-tab actions on sessions 1 and 2 with no dialog, each original session removed, and a native secondary click in the inactive raw pane changing active session 3 to 4. The exact actions, absence of an intervening confirmation, session IDs, and draft destruction depend on that operator record and the source-level close/activation analysis. The static before/after PNGs alone cannot prove those temporal claims.
model-server.json reports normal stop with 0 model requests and 0 responses; both associated JSONL files are empty. This establishes no request reached that fixture server, not a network-wide claim. The operator reports no AI send or command submission during these reproductions; screenshots only corroborate visible idle/zero-block state.
App identity and manual-run.json record matching binary hashes at start/end, clean source at both points, and normal Flutter q exit code 0. These are capture metadata, not conclusions derived from the images.

CONCLUSION / LIMITS
The six originals consistently support the visible consequences of the two draft-close defects and the inactive-pane secondary-click activation defect. Combined with the explicitly attributed operator record and current source inspection, they are useful E1 failure-discovery evidence. They are not post-fix validation.
No full D2-T10, D2-T11, D2-T14, or other formal scenario is passed by this review. The run does not cover 12 tabs/reordering/pane movement, a cancellation-preservation path, pending-approval marks, all transient focus/PTY behavior, or multi-display DPR changes. The six stills cannot establish a continuous no-confirmation interval; the reviewer has not independently assessed the recording contents.

